{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"radiosity as diffuse interreflection radiosity as diffuse interreflection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md","fileName":"Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CG Integration and Render Passes]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CG Integration and Render Passes","HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"radiosity as diffuse interreflection radiosity as diffuse interreflection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md","fileName":"Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection","heading":"Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Radiosity simulates diffuse light bouncing between surfaces, rather than only the illumination that reaches each surface directly. In the book's red-ball example, light first strikes the ball and then carries some of its red color onto a nearby white wall that receives no direct source light. This color bleed helps CG share a believable lighting environment with surrounding geometry. Radiosity can be combined with global or [[HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG]], but the terms describe different jobs: bounce calculation versus light-source representation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["CG Integration and Render Passes","HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"radiosity as diffuse interreflection radiosity as diffuse interreflection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md","fileName":"Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Radiosity as Diffuse Interreflection","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CG Integration and Render Passes","HDR Image-Based Lighting for CG","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}